-- KNOWN COMPILER BUG (found with Alan 3.0beta8, filed 2026-08-12).
--
-- This case is committed deliberately WITHOUT a .expected/.ifid so the suite
-- fails on it -- a standing reminder until the bug is fixed. When fixed, this
-- program should compile cleanly; then capture its output with `ok` to turn it
-- into a normal passing test.
--
-- THE BUG: an aggregate (SUM/MAX/MIN OF <attr> IN <container>) loses the
-- container's TAKING class when that taking class is ITSELF a container declared
-- with a bare CONTAINER (no Taking -> defaults to 'thing'). The compiler then
-- takes the guaranteed member class to be the JOIN of the two taking classes,
-- which collapses to 'thing', and rejects an attribute defined on the real
-- taking class:
--
--   316 E : Attribute 'cover' is not defined for instances aggregated over
--           using 'SUM' since the class it is guaranteed to be in this
--           context ('thing') does not have it.
--
-- Below, 'closet' TAKES garment and 'cover' is defined on garment, so
-- 'SUM OF cover IN closet' is valid and SHOULD compile. Removing garment's bare
-- CONTAINER (or narrowing it to 'Taking garment') makes it compile -- which
-- proves the TAKING narrowing is exactly what is being dropped.
--
-- Found while play-testing the Wyldkynd game: EVERY clothing had a bare CONTAINER
-- ("to allow a wallet in a jacket"), which broke the library's
-- SUM OF topcover IN worn (worn CONTAINER TAKING clothing).

The room Isa location
End the.

The hero Isa actor At room
  Is total 0.
End the.

The closet Isa entity
  Container Taking garment.
End the.

Every garment Isa thing
  Is cover 0.
  Container            -- bare container (defaults to Taking thing): the trigger
End every.

Verb probe
  Does
    Set total Of hero To Sum Of cover In closet.
End verb.

Start At room.
